 "method": "Compare each country's annual wind total across the sources that report it.  The reference is Eurostat's gross electricity production where Eurostat covers the country, and Ember otherwise. The bands follow the PyVWF scorecard audit: a ratio within 0.85-1.15 of the reference agrees, 0.70-1.30 is noted, and anything further out is flagged. Gross production runs above what transmission operators meter, so ratios a little under 1 are normal; the entry's traps usually say why. Fleets under 0.05 TWh a year are compared but not judged, because rounding alone moves their ratio. Ember and Eurostat compile national figures, so an exact match can mean the same upstream data rather than independent confirmation; the check catches a series that measures only part of a fleet, not a shared error.",
